      "writtenOn": "2020-10-28T22:36:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1. The organization of this function is getting a bit hard to follow intuitively. How about something like this?\n\nif (usb4_state \u003d\u003d USB4_INACTIVE)\n  return false;\n\nif (SOP ID doesn\u0027t support USB4)\n  return false;\n\nif (passive cable) {\n  if (speed too low)\n    return false;\n} else if (active cable) {\n  if (high VDM/VDO versions and cable does not support USB4)\n    return false;\n  else /* low VDM versions */ {\n    if (does not support TBT and TBT entry is not done)\n      return false;\n  }\n}\n\n2. The entire cable section could also be its own function (perhaps expanding enter_usb_cable_is_capable). I think that might improve things, because the TCPM and partner state work best as return-false-early, but the cable state might be clearer as return-true-early.",
